<h2>What our privacy policy says we collect</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>What you give us:</strong> account and profile data, contact details, ticket and booking data, support messages, preferences and content you post.</li>
<li><strong>Payments:</strong> limited payment information such as masked card numbers and transaction identifiers. Full card details are typically handled by payment processors and not stored by us.</li>
<li><strong>Collected automatically:</strong> device and browser information, usage data, approximate location from your IP address, and cookies and similar technologies.</li>
<li><strong>From others:</strong> event organizers, payment processors, advertising and analytics partners, sign-in providers and public sources.</li>
</ul>

<h2>How the privacy policy says we use and share data</h2>
<p>The policy lists these uses: running your account and ticket orders, customer support, personalization, marketing and advertising, analytics and improvement, and security and fraud prevention. It also covers legal and dispute purposes.</p>
<p>We may share information with event organizers and venues, service providers such as payment and hosting companies, group companies, authorities where required, in a business transfer, or with your consent. Organizers can act as independent controllers, so their own privacy policies may also apply.</p>

<h2>Your rights under the privacy policy</h2>
<p>Depending on where you live, the policy says you may have rights to access, correct, delete, restrict, port or object to the use of your data, to withdraw consent, and to complain to a data protection authority. To use them, email privacy@seatoutlet.com. We may need to verify your identity first.</p>
<ul>
<li>Unsubscribe from marketing with the link in any marketing email, or change preferences in your account settings where available.</li>
<li>Service messages, such as booking confirmations and security alerts, may still be sent.</li>
<li>Manage cookies in your browser, device settings or any cookie tool on the platform.</li>
</ul>
<div class="so-callout"><p>The policy also notes that no method of transmission or storage is completely secure, and that you are responsible for keeping your login details confidential.</p></div>

